  "description": "The attach redraw wiggle (5.46; PTY §7.2): after every attach the core sends the target one resize pair — cols−1 then cols — so a full-screen app answers with a redraw. It is a broker action, never a client request, so it is outside 5.50's request/reply path and is never answered with a C2 size frame. Every attach at this tag needs one, because 5.50 §4 makes no attach a size request, so PTY §7.2's 'an attach that does change the size needs none' has no case here. It does not fire while any stale choice is pending (gap or grid_lost, 5.52) or with the knob off; and it never sends cols below common.cols's minimum — at the minimum it goes one column wider then back (F20). Each resize reaches the target as its own window-change, in order; a worker never coalesces two. Graded against the frozen v0.2 wheel and the harness rig (owed).",
  "corpus": [
    "5.46",
    "5.50 §4",
    "PTY §7.2",
    "immortality §5.3",
    "plan.md §3 C3"
  ],
